{:spec/title "The policy gate blocks on judge findings in the forms a change edits, not on a touched file's older debt"

 :spec/description
 "`:policy-verify` and `:policy-review`
  (`ai.miniforge.gate.policy-pack/check-policy-pack-for-phase`) send each
  changed file's whole content to the batched LLM judge, and every finding
  of an acting rule (`:hard-halt` or `:require-approval`) blocks. A file the
  change touches must therefore reach zero findings in every form, including
  forms the change never edited. Most source files on main fail that: the
  judge reports acting findings in each of the ten files sampled on
  2026-11-05, `policy_pack.clj` and `no_secrets.clj` among them. That day a
  dogfood run edited one function in `runner_environment.clj`, was blocked by
  findings elsewhere in the file, and spread into callers and tests, each with
  findings of their own, until it failed. The `:no-secrets` gate already
  reports only matches that touch added lines.

  Change:
  1. For each changed file the gate finds the lines the change adds, and the
     points where it deletes lines, by diffing the artifact's content against
     the base blob of its path. The base is the first of `:code/base-refs`,
     `:execution/task-base-refs` and the environment's base SHA that
     resolves; never HEAD, which holds the change once the implement phase
     commits.
  2. In a Clojure source or EDN file the edited region is every top-level
     form that holds an added line or a pure removal, or that directly
     follows removed lines starting with `^` or `#_` (removing a reader
     prefix such as `^:private` changes the next form), plus each added line
     outside any form. In any other file it is the added lines.
  3. A judge finding on a line inside the edited region blocks as today. A
     finding outside it becomes a gate warning that says it lies outside the
     change, and does not block.
  4. Anything the gate cannot place blocks as today: a finding with no line,
     line 0 or a line past the file's last; a file with no worktree or base
     to diff against; content that does not parse; or a git command that
     fails. A new file has every line
     added, so all of its findings block."

 :spec/intent
 {:type :bugfix
  :scope ["components/gate/src/ai/miniforge/gate"
          "components/gate/test/ai/miniforge/gate"
          "components/gate/resources/config/gate/messages"
          "components/gate/deps.edn"]}

 :spec/constraints
 ["Only LLM-judge findings are scoped; deterministic detectors keep evaluating the whole artifact"
  "The judge still receives the whole file; scoping applies to its findings, not its input"
  "The base and diff helpers are shared with :no-secrets, not copied"
  "Rule evidence keeps the N3 statuses: a rule with findings only outside the change is still :failed"
  "The outside-the-change warning text goes through the gate message catalog"]

 :spec/acceptance-criteria
 ["Given a base file with forms A and B and a change that edits only A, a judge finding on a line of B passes the gate and appears in its warnings"
  "In the same change, a judge finding on a line of A fails the gate and appears in its errors"
  "A finding on an added line between two top-level forms blocks"
  "A change that only deletes lines inside form A makes a finding in A block"
  "In a file with no base blob, a finding on any line blocks"
  "A change that only removes a ^:private line above form B makes a finding in B block"
  "A change that replaces the line directly above form B, removing no reader prefix, leaves a finding in B a warning"
  "A finding with line 0, no line, or a line past the file's last blocks"
  "With no worktree path, every finding blocks"
  "A finding in a file whose content does not parse blocks"
  "Top-level form spans are found in a namespace that uses #?(:clj ...), ::alias/kw with an alias the reader cannot resolve, #inst, and an unknown tagged literal"
  "The existing :no-secrets and policy-pack gate tests pass after the shared helpers move"]

 :spec/priority
 {:tier :blocker
  :axes #{:dogfood-enabler :correctness}
  :theme :policy-enforcement
  :rationale "Every dogfood run that touches an existing file must first clear that file's older debt, so runs spread past their spec's scope and fail."
  :blocks []
  :blocked-by []}

 :spec/workflow-type :canonical-sdlc}
